{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time","id":1546865,"title":"Damage over time","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-11T07:23:57-08:00","id":1546865,"title":"Damage over time","content":"Are there any rules for magical damege over time?<br /> Personally i homebrew the durations of spells but im interested how in RAW does a spell that lights someone on fire (dealing dmg) constantly for lets say a day work mechanically. Cant find it in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T07:57:18-08:00","id":1546867,"title":"","content":"It's on page 538 in M20. But it's not written for turn by turn ongoing damage. Instead it is for longer term damage over time spells, and in addition to duration you have to pay successes for each interval within that duration. Keep in mind, though that the first level of duration takes it to one scene, which automatically makes it longer than a spell that lasts for a few turns.<br /> <br /> For setting someone on fire, I'd just default to the actual fire rules for as long as the spell keeps them on fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T16:08:01-08:00","id":1546881,"title":"","content":"Certain sorts of damaging effects will also impose damage over a longer period of time, just because of what sort of damage it is. This is mostly in the realm of secondary effects, such as using higher level Forces or Matter effects to create poisons or radiation, or Life effects which influence the spread of disease or simulate particular conditions.<br /> <br /> Being able to do this sort of thing depends heavily on understanding what you're trying to create or impose well enough to produce it with the appropriate effects, and that's reflected by one sort of skill or another. If you want to give someone radiation poisoning, you do need to have some good understanding of what radiation <i>is</i>, as knowledge of Forces and Prime by itself doesn't impart an understanding of such phenomena. (If a character has directly observed radiation of some sort using Forces perception, they might well be able to simply copy that pattern to produce it, but they won't necessarily fully understand the practical effects of what they're playing with.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 12-11-2024, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T20:33:16-08:00","id":1546888,"title":"","content":"It still very quickly turns right back into the same thing as just lighting someone on fire and using the normal fire rules for it. While the WoD never made radioactivity a core book hazard, poisons and toxins generally are, as are diseases. If I use magic to ensure a cobra bites someone, the book has rules for snake bites after the magic has lead to the result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-12T18:56:06-08:00","id":1546912,"title":"","content":"Yes, normal fire would hurt, yes.<br /> <br /> But what about magic fire?<br /> <br /> Ok, let's change the scenario a bit:<br /> <br /> Imagine I create Sunlight to give a little tan to a vampire in the middle of the night.<br /> <br /> And, that light will last for a full scene. Then what?<br /> <br /> Or I throw a can of &quot;grey goo&quot; at a target - that is, flesh eating nanobots... That, presumably, deal &quot;X amount of damage per turn&quot;.<br /> <br /> If I turn off the &quot;magic&quot;, the &quot;nanobots&quot; cease to function... Do you know what I mean?<br /> <br /> I guess that's more in line with what OP was asking","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T00:50:48-08:00","id":1546916,"title":"","content":"I could be wrong, but I'd assume the OP (given references in other threads) is somewhat inspired by the way Awakening 2e handles this, as Awakening has a concrete mechanical answer to the question where Ascension does not.<br /> <br /> IME though, offensively it tends to be overkill in either game; save a small niche of when you're effectively trying to nullify another supernatural's healing abilities by causing them enough damage over time that you follow up attacks don't get healed and thus you don't get stuck being ineffectual in net damage. Defense tends to be a better use case for characters without the oomph to give themselves werewolf-esque levels of regeneration, but can give themselves significantly better healing than humans would have coupled with not having to consciously activate it each time. <br /> <br /> What happens in Ascension if you heal yourself for 4 damage but extend the duration to a day has no real answer, and there isn't something equivalent like blast a vampire with sunlight magically where you can just point to the VtM rules for sunlight exposure to dictate what happens next. <br /> <br /> As it stands, Ascension doesn't have any sample rules that really offers any suggestions on how to handle an effect that's between &quot;single instant casting that heals X damage and that's that (maybe a conditional hung spell so it happens when you need it later),&quot; and, &quot;high level Life magic for full super-regeneration.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T04:12:32-08:00","id":1546920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1546916#post1546916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could be wrong, but I'd assume the OP (given references in other threads) is somewhat inspired by the way Awakening 2e handles this, as Awakening has a concrete mechanical answer to the question where Ascension does not.<br /> <br /> IME though, offensively it tends to be overkill in either game; save a small niche of when you're effectively trying to nullify another supernatural's healing abilities by causing them enough damage over time that you follow up attacks don't get healed and thus you don't get stuck being ineffectual in net damage. Defense tends to be a better use case for characters without the oomph to give themselves werewolf-esque levels of regeneration, but can give themselves significantly better healing than humans would have coupled with not having to consciously activate it each time.<br /> <br /> What happens in Ascension if you heal yourself for 4 damage but extend the duration to a day has no real answer, and there isn't something equivalent like blast a vampire with sunlight magically where you can just point to the VtM rules for sunlight exposure to dictate what happens next.<br /> <br /> As it stands, Ascension doesn't have any sample rules that really offers any suggestions on how to handle an effect that's between &quot;single instant casting that heals X damage and that's that (maybe a conditional hung spell so it happens when you need it later),&quot; and, &quot;high level Life magic for full super-regeneration.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, i know both games but i mainly use ascension.<br /> Im looking for some rules of dot turn by turn dmg. Could also be rules to passively heal turn by turn. For example a decaying curse that deals 3 dmg each turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T05:41:09-08:00","id":1546922,"title":"","content":"As I said, there aren't any general rules for DoT (or whatever over time) magic in Ascension. The best you get are magically inducing existing DoT mechanics and perhaps enhancing them for ones that are slower than 1/turn (like using magic to speed or slow the rate of disease/poison/toxin rolls depending on what you'd want to have happen to the target).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T20:08:39-08:00","id":1546951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1546920#post1546920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not really, i know both games but i mainly use ascension.<br /> Im looking for some rules of dot turn by turn dmg. Could also be rules to passively heal turn by turn. For example a decaying curse that deals 3 dmg each turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1546922#post1546922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, there aren't any general rules for DoT (or whatever over time) magic in Ascension. The best you get are magically inducing existing DoT mechanics and perhaps enhancing them for ones that are slower than 1/turn (like using magic to speed or slow the rate of disease/poison/toxin rolls depending on what you'd want to have happen to the target).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's it, Heavy Arms is right. There aren't rules for that, you'll just have to houserule it. I would go with two successes per damage per turn, that's just a suggestion. It would need some testing thou. But I believe that this would be the bare minimum, since extending such an effect for a single day would pretty much guarantee the kill.<br /> <br /> There are tons of considerations to make thou that could change this math: the damage could be per minute instead of per turn, or per hour, per day, per week, month, maybe even yearly, like a sort of &quot;permanent injury&quot; curse. I admit I don't have a good answer for all these permutations <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T01:43:15-08:00","id":1546955,"title":"","content":"Then ill go with:<br /> \u2022 Each Scene interval = one success<br /> \u2022 Each day interval = two successes<br /> \u2022 Each story interval = three successes<br /> \u2022 Each six-month interval = four successes<br /> <br /> and on micro scale:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Each hour interval = one success<br /> \u2022 Each minute interval = two successes<br /> \u2022 Each turn interval = four successes<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T10:55:43-08:00","id":1546970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1546955#post1546955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then ill go with:<br /> \u2022 Each Scene interval = one success<br /> \u2022 Each day interval = two successes<br /> \u2022 Each story interval = three successes<br /> \u2022 Each six-month interval = four successes<br /> <br /> and on micro scale:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Each hour interval = one success<br /> \u2022 Each minute interval = two successes<br /> \u2022 Each turn interval = four successes<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's probably a good start worth of testing. For massive &quot;degenerative curses&quot; it would require massive rituals to be performed, thus it can't be used in combat, and that's fair; causing 5 damage per turn for an entire day is hugely massive after all (60 min per hour, 60 seconds per minute, 24 hours per day, just do the math). Even a single point of damage per turn is quite a lot, even if its soakable, because for an entire day there will be enough failures (and critical failures) to kill anyone that hasn't some sort of magic mambo jambo protection","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T15:24:46-08:00","id":1547522,"title":"","content":"I know a lot of people don't like &quot;How do You Do That?&quot;, mysellf included (although it does have some good, very usable rules), but it does have rules for damage over time<br /> <br /> P.37<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If, for example, Chopper wants to set up a super-cold wall of ice that lasts one day and inflicts six levels of damage to anyone who touches it, her player would need to roll a total of six successes: three for the Duration, three for the Damage. Remember that the Forces Sphere automatically adds one success to the Damage. If Chopper decides to make that wall of plasma-energy (Forces) rather than ice (Matter), she needs only five successes because one success is already taken care of by the Forces Sphere. </div> </div> </div>The examples are for ice and plasma walls, but the logic would apply in your examples as well, I guess.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems the damage would apply everytime someone touches it, so it would deal that X damage each round.<br /> It seems a bit excessive, but that is Mage\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T15:55:46-08:00","id":1547524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547522#post1547522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know a lot of people don't like &quot;How do You Do That?&quot;, mysellf included (although it does have some good, very usable rules), but it does have rules for damage over time<br /> <br /> P.37<br /> <br /> <br /> The examples are for ice and plasma walls, but the logic would apply in your examples as well, I guess.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems the damage would apply everytime someone touches it, so it would deal that X damage each round.<br /> It seems a bit excessive, but that is Mage\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats not damage over time, thats 1 time damage from touching the wall.<br /> I would call that a ward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 01-04-2025, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T18:45:58-08:00","id":1547527,"title":"","content":"It's kinda damage over time in the sense of you taking damage every turn your touch the icy wall of doom. That section references back to the hazardous environments rules from the core book though... rather than having specific DoT rules for magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T06:39:45-08:00","id":1547541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547527#post1547527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's kinda damage over time in the sense of you taking damage every turn your touch the icy wall of doom. That section references back to the hazardous environments rules from the core book though... rather than having specific DoT rules for magic</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno about that, Reading from the mechanical side of things we have a few possibilities:<br /> <br /> 1. Someone used the rules for damage intervals from the main rulebook. If so it is calculated wrongly as once a day is 1 success not 3.<br /> <br /> 2. They did not intend for it to be a dot but rather a sort of ward that may be interactable only when touched. Similar to how wards are done in blood magic vtm where if you ward a staff against vampires then it damages a vampire only if the vampire touches it willingly instead of activating every time someon hits him with it.<br /> <br /> 3. Someone did not predict this may be used as a dot and it is just writen wrong.<br /> <br /> 4. Thats how the creators intended the dots to work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T07:06:22-08:00","id":1547542,"title":"","content":"5. It is treated as a weapon enchancment (like a sword with added elemental damage). In this case it cant be treated as a dot effect on someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T08:56:59-08:00","id":1547547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547524#post1547524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats not damage over time, thats 1 time damage from touching the wall.<br /> I would call that a ward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it is damage over time. What happens if someone keeps touching the plasma wall? Or if someone is trapped inside an ice wall with a spherical shape? The damage would apply every turm. Again, I too think it's an overkill, but this is Mage. Also, you need double the successes to make it last a day, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T09:03:04-08:00","id":1547548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547541#post1547541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno about that, Reading from the mechanical side of things we have a few possibilities:<br /> <br /> 1. Someone used the rules for damage intervals from the main rulebook. If so it is calculated wrongly as once a day is 1 success not 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 duration chart is<br /> <br /> 1 success: 1 turn<br /> 2 successes: a scene<br /> 3 successes: a day<br /> <br /> So, for 6 damage over 1 day, you need 6 successes, just like HDYDT explained (3 dor damage+3 for duration).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547541#post1547541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. They did not intend for it to be a dot but rather a sort of ward that may be interactable only when touched. Similar to how wards are done in blood magic vtm where if you ward a staff against vampires then it damages a vampire only if the vampire touches it willingly instead of activating every time someon hits him with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if someone pushes the vampire into the plasma wall (he wasn't going willingly), then there is no damage applied? That makes no sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547541#post1547541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Someone did not predict this may be used as a dot and it is just writen wrong.<br /> <br /> 4. Thats how the creators intended the dots to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably one of those 2. We can't know for sure. I'm just providing a raw rule, since no one did. I still think it's not necessarily overpowered. I mean, if you want to make it in a way that the target can't escape the damage, you would need more successes? Depending on exactly what the spell does. The plasma wall can easily be avoided, unless the Mage casts another spell to force the target there, which is a hole new scenario...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T14:06:16-08:00","id":1547557,"title":"","content":"It treats these things like creating a fire, but you control the shape. HDYDT? directly references the hazardous environment rules such as fires and electrocution in that section. If you stick you hands in a flame, you take damage per turn until you pull your hands out of the flame. &quot;Plasma&quot; (fire is in a plasma state anyway), electricity, ice, or whatever... it doesn't really make a difference to the concept of &quot;wall of stuff that hurts if you touch it, so don't touch it.&quot; It doesn't have a magic-based interval because conceptually it's not magically hurting you every X amount of time. The damage is inherent to the nature of the effect (again, just like magically created fire doesn't need to have a magic derived DoT interval if someone sticks their hands in the flames), the magic is just the duration of the effect and how dangerous it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T16:04:54-08:00","id":1547561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547557#post1547557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It treats these things like creating a fire, but you control the shape. HDYDT? directly references the hazardous environment rules such as fires and electrocution in that section. If you stick you hands in a flame, you take damage per turn until you pull your hands out of the flame. &quot;Plasma&quot; (fire is in a plasma state anyway), electricity, ice, or whatever... it doesn't really make a difference to the concept of &quot;wall of stuff that hurts if you touch it, so don't touch it.&quot; It doesn't have a magic-based interval because conceptually it's not magically hurting you every X amount of time. The damage is inherent to the nature of the effect (again, just like magically created fire doesn't need to have a magic derived DoT interval if someone sticks their hands in the flames), the magic is just the duration of the effect and how dangerous it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is certainly an option, it would not require successes on duration. When you cast a fireball explosion (instant spell), it can catch things on fire and that fire (regular, not magickal) will burn and damage over time.<br /> <br /> But when you spend successes into duration, the fire that will burn for that duration is not regular fire anymore, it is magickal fire. This is clear by the example in hdydt, since regular ice does not deal 6 levels of damage on touch.<br /> <br /> Of course, one can try and magickally put out the fire or break the wall or juat avoid the area. So it's not a hit kill spell as it seems?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T17:05:53-08:00","id":1547564,"title":"","content":"My point is that a wall of fire and a wall of ice are, mechanically, nearly identical for the HDYDT? example. I get that a fireball can light flammable things on fire too, but I'm trying to help and reinforce your point, not contradict it.<br /> <br /> (Though cold can kill just as fast as hot can, it's just much harder to get that kind of cold in average human-friendly conditions, and using an ice wall is very inefficient against humans when talking about normal physics)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T17:33:40-08:00","id":1547565,"title":"","content":"I see. I was just pointing out the differences. While a fire/ice spell would follow the damage/duration chart, natural elements would follow the hazard rules, which are way weaker.<br /> <br /> But regarding the working, yes, they are quite similar as they deal damage each turn. i can't see the ice wall example working any other way\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T03:05:49-08:00","id":1547574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547565#post1547565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. I was just pointing out the differences. While a fire/ice spell would follow the damage/duration chart, natural elements would follow the hazard rules, which are way weaker.<br /> <br /> But regarding the working, yes, they are quite similar as they deal damage each turn. i can't see the ice wall example working any other way\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Then i see this more like a weapon enchantment thing, like making a fire sword. In this case this cannot be cast directly on enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T03:35:46-08:00","id":1547575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547574#post1547574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then i see this more like a weapon enchantment thing, like making a fire sword. In this case this cannot be cast directly on enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it has nothing to do with enchanting weapons. It is a damage spell with a duration. That's it. You can cast a plasma wall in the exact spot where is an enemy, but he can always get the hell out of there (unless you somehow trap him there?). The firts turn should deal damage, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T04:24:07-08:00","id":1547577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547575#post1547575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it has nothing to do with enchanting weapons. It is a damage spell with a duration. That's it. You can cast a plasma wall in the exact spot where is an enemy, but he can always get the hell out of there (unless you somehow trap him there?). The firts turn should deal damage, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is literally game breaking, Why spend 6 successes on damage when you can use 3 on dmg and 3 on duration to enchant dirrectly the enemy (or his clothes) to take infinite more damage (just streched a bit longer in time).<br /> Or even not 3 duration, a minute for 1 success would be enough to slay a god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 01-06-2025, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T07:01:44-08:00","id":1547579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547577#post1547577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is literally game breaking, Why spend 6 successes on damage when you can use 3 on dmg and 3 on duration to enchant dirrectly the enemy (or his clothes) to take infinite more damage (just streched a bit longer in time).<br /> Or even not 3 duration, a minute for 1 success would be enough to slay a god.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im not sure you can cast an area of effect spell on an object or person. Or at least it would require more successes and/or spheres to lock the spell.<br /> <br /> But yeah, it is very powerful, but so is magick. An Arete 3 mage that spends WP can deal 10 agg damage in a single turn with ease. Combat and damage shouldn't be the main thing in the setting, I guess. <br /> <br /> Also, the very example in HDYDT says that with 6 successes you deal 6 damage for anyone touching the wall, (5 successes with Forces), so there isn't much room to deny it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T07:20:56-08:00","id":1547580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547579#post1547579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im not sure you can cast an area of effect spell on an object or person. Or at least it would require more successes and/or spheres to lock the spell.<br /> <br /> But yeah, it is very powerful, but so is magick. An Arete 3 mage that spends WP can deal 10 agg damage in a single turn with ease. Combat and damage shouldn't be the main thing in the setting, I guess.<br /> <br /> Also, the very example in HDYDT says that with 6 successes you deal 6 damage for anyone touching the wall, (5 successes with Forces), so there isn't much room to deny it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah HDYDT does many things wrong so nothing new.<br /> <br /> Magic is powerful but this is more powerful than any other magic if interpreted that way.<br /> <br /> My theory is someone did not predict this could be interpreted as a dot. Thats why i would call it an enchancment that increases the damage of something (area for example) but cant really hurt the thing its locked to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T08:16:48-08:00","id":1547582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547580#post1547580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah HDYDT does many things wrong so nothing new.<br /> <br /> Magic is powerful but this is more powerful than any other magic if interpreted that way.<br /> <br /> My theory is someone did not predict this could be interpreted as a dot. Thats why i would call it an enchancment that increases the damage of something (area for example) but cant really hurt the thing its locked to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your point makes no sense. The examples are for walls that deals damage, not a weapon enchantment. Even if you forbid any variation of this effect, the very examples would still deal a lot of damage. What's stopping the mage to cast a plasma wall right on top of the enemy, or trapping the enemy in place and casting the wall? It would still deal 6 damage as long as the target is in contact with the wall.<br /> <br /> You can always use HR, I'm just providing a raw rule and examples.<br /> <br /> The truth is, if the game is very combat oriented, the ST *will* have to deal with mages dealing a LOT of damage (which they can do easily). Probably with immunity/reduction of a certain element, or counterspells, idk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T09:01:39-08:00","id":1547590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547582#post1547582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your point makes no sense. The examples are for walls that deals damage, not a weapon enchantment. Even if you forbid any variation of this effect, the very examples would still deal a lot of damage. What's stopping the mage to cast a plasma wall right on top of the enemy, or trapping the enemy in place and casting the wall? It would still deal 6 damage as long as the target is in contact with the wall.<br /> <br /> You can always use HR, I'm just providing a raw rule and examples.<br /> <br /> The truth is, if the game is very combat oriented, the ST *will* have to deal with mages dealing a LOT of damage (which they can do easily). Probably with immunity/reduction of a certain element, or counterspells, idk.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is you can escale from a wall appearing on you you can even do a dodge, when its your clothes or you you cant escape it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T09:24:59-08:00","id":1547592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547590#post1547590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference is you can escale from a wall appearing on you you can even do a dodge, when its your clothes or you you cant escape it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree. However, you can't just choose to cast on clothes. The mage would *at least* need Matter to lock on the clothes (which can be desperately removed by the target) and possibly require more successes by the ST. <br /> The mage can also cast the wall on a small space where the target can't escape or immobilize the target somehow. All of that would depend on the scenario at hand.<br /> <br /> But the point still stands, by the examples raw, the wall would deal a lot of damage each turn and all the ST can do is use a HR (which I personally don't like very much) or deal with it in-game with some protection for the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T09:26:33-08:00","id":1547593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547592#post1547592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I agree. However, you can't just choose to cast on clothes. The mage would *at least* need Matter to lock on the clothes (which can be desperately removed by the target) and possibly require more successes by the ST.<br /> The mage can also cast the wall on a small space where the target can't escape or immobilize the target somehow. All of that would depend on the scenario at hand.<br /> <br /> But the point still stands, by the examples raw, the wall would deal a lot of damage each turn and all the ST can do is use a HR (which I personally don't like very much) or deal with it in-game with some protection for the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again i think there is a difference between a wall and a dot.<br /> the wall is the source of damage and its physical, the dot interacts dirrectly on the target","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T11:10:04-08:00","id":1547594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547593#post1547593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again i think there is a difference between a wall and a dot.<br /> the wall is the source of damage and its physical, the dot interacts dirrectly on the target</div> </div> </div> </div>What you mean by a dot?<br /> <br /> By physical so you mean tangible? Because the wall can be made of plasma, electricity, fire, etc. and you can create a wall with any shape anywhere (including on top of the target).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T11:49:20-08:00","id":1547597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547579#post1547579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, it is very powerful, but so is magick. An Arete 3 mage that spends WP can deal 10 agg damage in a single turn with ease.</div> </div> </div> </div>This really needs to be addressed more. The issue with DoT (Damage over Time) in Mage, is that most targets only have 7 HLs, and doing 8+ damage is not that hard to do in one shot.<br /> <br /> As I said earlier in the thread, DoT in Mage is overkill. If you can get enough successes to do serious DoT, you can get enough successes to just kill the target outright anyway. As well, in the WoD, &quot;toughness&quot; tends to mean soak and regeneration/potent healing. If you want to kill a werewolf, spending 6 successes to do 12 damage in one shot is a better bet than 6 DoT because werewolves have high soak that might negate 6 damage completely, or reduce it enough that they can regenerate the rest during the interval.<br /> <br /> Calling the HDYDT? rules &quot;overpowered&quot; is kinda forgetting how powerful direct attacks in Mage can be. There's a reason why Porthos didn't do some fancy wall of fire when confronted with an armada of VE Voidships.... he just exploded them all in a gigantic archmage of Forces blast of doom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T12:06:27-08:00","id":1547600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546865-damage-over-time?p=1547597#post1547597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This really needs to be addressed more. The issue with DoT (Damage over Time) in Mage, is that most targets only have 7 HLs, and doing 8+ damage is not that hard to do in one shot.<br /> <br /> As I said earlier in the thread, DoT in Mage is overkill. If you can get enough successes to do serious DoT, you can get enough successes to just kill the target outright anyway. As well, in the WoD, &quot;toughness&quot; tends to mean soak and regeneration/potent healing. If you want to kill a werewolf, spending 6 successes to do 12 damage in one shot is a better bet than 6 DoT because werewolves have high soak that might negate 6 damage completely, or reduce it enough that they can regenerate the rest during the interval.<br /> <br /> Calling the HDYDT? rules &quot;overpowered&quot; is kinda forgetting how powerful direct attacks in Mage can be. There's a reason why Porthos didn't do some fancy wall of fire when confronted with an armada of VE Voidships.... he just exploded them all in a gigantic archmage of Forces blast of doom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with everything you said and you made very solid points. The werewolf in question could also just get away from that place (unless the mage somehow locks the effect on him, which means Forces+Prime+Life+Spirit) AND the werewolf can counterspell by M20 rules, iirc (have to check if it can be done in ongoing effects).<br /> <br /> Yeah, doing 8+ aggravated in a single turn is easy even for an initial mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T14:02:56-08:00","id":1548374,"title":"","content":"Found this :<br /> &quot;Like damage, an Effect\u2019s duration is based upon the successes<br /> you roll; the better you roll, the longer your spell lasts. This<br /> applies, of course, to spells that could potentially last a while \u2013<br /> charms, enhanced perceptions, shape-changing, and so forth.<br /> Damage-based attacks tend to be immediate, whereas attacks that<br /> change the target without causing health level injuries follow the<br /> Duration part of theDamage or Duration chart.<br /> As mentioned on that chart, you can either inflict<br /> immediate damage (in which case Duration is one turn) or else<br /> cast a spell that lasts awhile (in which case Damage is zero).<br /> The only way to inflict damage over a period of time involves<br /> the Divided Successes option.&quot;<br /> rulebook page 543","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-17T13:39:54-08:00","id":1548556,"title":"","content":"I would handle DoT effects this way<br /> <br /> (TL;DR: Roll damage as usual. Roll duration of effect. Then place finger onto that entry in the duration table. Slide finger one entry downward! Yay that number there (Let's call it X!) tells us the successess required per DoT interval! Slide finger up again for every X DoT Successess you roll to determine DoT interval!)<br /> <br /> <br /> You need:<br /> <br /> 1) Base + Damage successes as usual<br /> 2) Duration successes to determine the total duration of the effect.<br /> 3) DoT interval successes. They count back *down* the duration Table, they start one higher than the current Duration entry and require (Duration successes + 1) per step down towards the smaller entries. If your Duration is 4 (Story) you start the DoT interval at 5 (6 months) and try to move the bar towards the smaller entries.<br /> <br /> Remider, here's the Duration table:<br /> 1 - Turn<br /> 2- Scene<br /> 3 - Day<br /> 4 - Story<br /> 5 - Six months<br /> 6 - ???<br /> <br /> Example of a DoT roll pile:<br /> 1 base succ = Target other than you<br /> 3 damage succs = 6 damage<br /> 3 Duration succs = 1 day.<br /> <br /> Alright, the effect lasts a day, but now we have to handle the actual DoT Interval...<br /> <br /> Now, here come the DoT successes:<br /> Our duration is '3 - Day' so we start at the '4 - Story' entry. Well darnit, that won't give us any DoT effect at all!<br /> Time to push the DoT slider towards the smaller entries: We need 4 successes (Due to our 3 duration successes + 1) to make the DoT interval be 'Day' for this effect.<br /> 4 more than that to make it 'Scene', etc.<br /> <br /> 4 DoT succs -&gt; 6 damage at 1-day intervals. Which means this hits a total of 2 times: At the very start of the effect, and the very end. Meh.<br /> 8 DoT succs -&gt; We jump up the table one step. 6 damage per scene.<br /> 12 DoT Succs -&gt; We are now on a turn-by-turn basis.<br /> <br /> Overpowered? Mind you ,this would normally translate to, oh *36 instant damage* if you didn't bother with a DoT, but hey. Maybe there is a reason.<br /> This way, dropping damage constantly for half a year also takes 30 DoT successes, which is pretty much approaching a godlike feat, as well as a horrendous waste of a mage's resources, given how much damage that could deal immediately.<br /> But Hey, maybe some special threat warrants it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 02-17-2025, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}